Description: Don't resolve an apphost for excluded Helix projects in source-build
 The Helix JobMonitor tool (OutputType=Exe, net8.0) is still restored even
 though Helix is excluded from source-only builds. Restore resolves an apphost
 for the host RID, which fails with NETSDK1084 on linux-riscv64 because .NET 8
 has no riscv64 apphost. Regression introduced in 10.0.114.
Author: Adeel Mujahid (am11)
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/dotnet/dotnet/pull/11284
Bug: https://github.com/dotnet/dotnet/issues/11013
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/src/arcade/src/Microsoft.DotNet.Helix/Directory.Build.props
+++ b/src/arcade/src/Microsoft.DotNet.Helix/Directory.Build.props
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@
   <!-- Exclude Helix from source-build until we find a reason to use it. -->
   <PropertyGroup>
     <ExcludeFromSourceOnlyBuild>true</ExcludeFromSourceOnlyBuild>
+    <!-- Excluded projects are still restored, which resolves an apphost for executables such as the
+         JobMonitor tool; source-build may have none for the target RID (e.g. linux-riscv64). -->
+    <UseAppHost Condition="'$(DotNetBuildSourceOnly)' == 'true'">false</UseAppHost>
   </PropertyGroup>
 
 </Project>
